  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_049 (scvi_n200, rna_only) achieved 0.520 acc, far outperforming config_045 (scgpt, rna_only) at 0.411. In multimodal, config_017 (scgpt + vit_l, weighted) gave only a marginal gain over scgpt alone (0.422 vs 0.411). The critical uncertainty is whether the image modality adds value when the RNA encoder is already strong (scvi_n200). This experiment (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, weighted, singleprofile) directly tests that question while keeping fusion and image encoder identical to config_017, isolating the RNA-encoder effect in the multimodal setting. If it substantially exceeds 0.520, multimodal with scvi_n200 is a promising direction to exploit; if it is near or below 0.520, we learn that image adds little and should redirect budget toward RNA-only multiprofile or aggregation experiments. This is the highest-information single step under the limited budget."
}

